{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786659661182064001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"pink-complex-xenurine","assignee":null,"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8cc0f347bc07ec1dfe88feceb3d39cde72563ce50051db3a66df01f9016e3636","event_uuid":"95e384d0-eda4-493c-9e59-fce17d09955c","position":{"commit_sha":"2bfca0f37405d765396ed68a91d9a889e7b0d53e","position":"1784760785255552001-95e384d0-eda4-493c-9e59-fce17d09955c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"70f63a541421c3618c0926ce67786cb53270f0b0a02765fb82d3291ada911dd6","event_uuid":"855f0671-2ac0-4016-83a9-bea24b3e552a","position":{"commit_sha":"84ab2fc484c217882adb79831c46c00b2aa63632","position":"1784760820728964001-855f0671-2ac0-4016-83a9-bea24b3e552a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cc5c95f2720a515b193c2757204eda9e6826673c3229863b5938db2e9342aa66","event_uuid":"2b619edc-cec6-44b8-9ba7-85e93bdd9b1c","position":{"commit_sha":"bce887cf98959cbb61d11d5fa5415ec73bb542e9","position":"1786550407237314844-2b619edc-cec6-44b8-9ba7-85e93bdd9b1c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1784760785255552001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"855f0671-2ac0-4016-83a9-bea24b3e552a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8559-44c3-e08a-4bb9"}],"description":"## Problem\nFindings carry a `severity` string (`severity_label(impact)` -> critical/major/minor/none,\n`review_kernel/decide.py`) that is derived from IMPACT ALONE, so it does not order the same way as\nthe authoritative `priority = validity x impact`. A high-impact/low-validity finding shows as\n`critical` while ranking below a `major`. This is a foot-gun: it invites reading the label as the\ngate signal when it is not. It also caused a field misread — via `_KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY`\n(major->high, minor->medium, none->info) the review-bot surfaced the same finding as INFO then\nMEDIUM across identical runs, reading like a severity change when only impact drifted.\n\n## Idea\nMake findings blocking / not-blocking + numeric priority, mirroring the intent that priority is\nthe single source of truth. Remove or rename the impact-only severity label so nothing mistakes it\nfor the decision.\n\n## Why this is NOT a one-liner (traced)\n- The label lives in the SHARED kernel (`pass3_decide`), so plan review carries it too — this is\n  not a code-review-only change.\n- The block/advisory decision is ALREADY binary and priority-keyed; severity is an extra surfaced\n  signal, not the gate.\n- Real consumers exist and there are TWO vocabularies (kernel critical/major/minor/none; and the\n  original 5-level critical/high/medium/low/info in `findings.py`, from commit b501c38d1):\n    - Gerrit review-bot comment surface (`review_bot/adapter.py`, ADR 0009)\n    - cross-finding aggregation/dedup picks the highest-severity representative (`aggregate.py`)\n    - workflow `fail_on_severity` policy (`workflow/steps.py`)\n\n## Suggested sequence (each independently reviewable)\n1. Rank aggregation by `priority` instead of severity.\n2. Surface `priority` + blocking/advisory in the review-bot instead of the mapped label.\n3. Migrate `fail_on_severity` to a priority threshold.\n4. Drop the `severity` field from the finding shape.\nChanges the Gerrit comment format and touches both gates -> warrants an ADR.\n\n## Provenance\nDiscovered from the upstream review-code false-positive report (client project). Sibling of the\nmerge-base diff fix (ticket 8559-44c3-e08a-4bb9).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"reconciler","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2b619edc-cec6-44b8-9ba7-85e93bdd9b1c","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Retire the kernel severity label in favor of numeric priority (blocking/not-blocking)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["95e384d0-eda4-493c-9e59-fce17d09955c","855f0671-2ac0-4016-83a9-bea24b3e552a","2b619edc-cec6-44b8-9ba7-85e93bdd9b1c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659661182064001,"uuid":"fdcb9e89-ba44-4b3a-8945-ba0b6284eb85"}